@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G5 · Borrow timelines: when the program stops using returned bytes
hide footbox
$caller(caller, "Program\n(caller)")
$callee(view, "view\nLibrary function")
$owner(store, "Store\nKeeps the bytes alive")
== Synthetic immutable store ==
caller --> view : At entry: lend the store to view
activate view
note over caller, view : Program keeps the input usable until view completes: valid($store, call).
view --> caller : At completion: lend access to the store's bytes
deactivate view
note over caller, store
  Program may keep reading the returned bytes while Store lives.
  The result says borrow(owner($store)).
  invalidated_by($result, []) names no earlier operation that ends this access.
end note
store ->x caller : Store is destroyed: program stops using the returned view
== Constructed mutable variant, separate from the fixture ==
caller --> view : At entry: lend the store to view
activate view
note over caller, view : Program keeps the input usable until view completes: valid($store, call).
view --> caller : At completion: lend access to the store's bytes
deactivate view
note over caller, store
  Program may read until replace starts or Store is destroyed, whichever comes first.
  Here replace starts first: invalidated_by($result, [@replace]).
end note
store ->x caller : replace starts: program stops using the old view
note over caller, store
  Store is still alive. The old view is already unusable,
  even if replace later fails.
end note
legend bottom
  Time runs downward within each separate case; spacing is not duration.
  Actor = caller; rectangle = callee; circle on base = owner; bar = active view call.
  Dashed arrow = borrowed access; marked end = invalidation, not caller destruction.
  The result's contract allows use after view completes. Non-normative: C1, C5.
  Other clauses and the mutable variant's full operation contracts are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
